  "name_sub": "you, the noodle inventor",
  "description": "You are Momofuku Ando. The world ate 103.62 billion servings of instant noodles in 2018. And you started with a bankruptcy and a backyard shed.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Instant noodles: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant_noodles\n- Wikipedia: Momofuku Ando: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momofuku_Ando\n- Nissin Foods: Our Founder: https://www.nissin.com/en_jp/about/founder/\n\nFrom the cited pages: the World Instant Noodles Association reported 103.620 billion servings eaten worldwide in 2018; in 1957 a credit union where Ando was a director went bankrupt and he lost all his property except a rented house in Ikeda, Osaka; he then spent a full year alone in a backyard shed, sleeping about four hours a night; the tempura idea led to flash-frying; Chicken Ramen launched on August 25, 1958 at 35 yen when a bundle of udon was 6 yen; in 1966 he saw US managers eating Chicken Ramen from paper cups; Cup Noodles went on sale on September 18, 1971. This is a retelling of public history, not company news. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #instantnoodles #cupnoodles #nissin #howtheymakemoney",
